# FH AECB Analyzer -- settings.
#
# On a server, copy to /etc/aecb-analyzer/aecb.env, fill in, and restrict it:
#   install -d -m 0750 /etc/aecb-analyzer
#   install -m 0600 -o aecb -g aecb deploy/aecb.env.example /etc/aecb-analyzer/aecb.env
# The systemd unit (deploy/aecb-analyzer.service) loads it with EnvironmentFile=.
#
# On a developer machine, copy to ~/etc/aecb-analyzer/aecb.env (mode 0600);
# app.py reads it at start-up (aecb/settings.py). Set AECB_ENV=dev and point
# the two folders below at your home folder as FULL paths -- values are taken
# literally, so ~ is not expanded (e.g. /Users/<you>/var/lib/aecb-analyzer/
# api_responses). See README.md.
#
# Never commit a filled-in copy.

# Bureau-report API service account (IIS Windows authentication, NTLMv2).
# Give the account and its Windows domain separately -- a backslash in this
# file would be read as an escape character.
AECB_API_USERNAME=svc_account
AECB_API_DOMAIN=DOMAIN
AECB_API_PASSWORD=

# Where each successful API response is archived (real bureau data). Must be
# OUTSIDE the application directory; created 0700 with files 0600. Leave
# unset to switch archiving off. Retention is an operations task
# (docs/OPERATIONS.md).
AECB_ARCHIVE_DIR=/var/lib/aecb-analyzer/api_responses

# Rotating application log (aecb.log). Unset: logs go to stderr / journald
# only.
AECB_LOG_DIR=/var/log/aecb-analyzer

# Optional: the request header an SSO reverse proxy sets to the authenticated
# user name, so each audit line records who queried which subject.
#AECB_AUDIT_USER_HEADER=X-Remote-User

# Which environment this server is: dev, uat or prod. It picks the AI Analysis's
# model provider (dev: the local Ollama model; uat/prod: Core42). Set uat on
# the UAT server. Unset means prod. dev is for developer machines only: it
# adds a sample picker and development tools to the app.
AECB_ENV=prod

# The AI panel: live, coming_soon or off. Unset on uat/prod means coming_soon
# -- the AI Analysis button shows "Coming soon" and no model is called.
# Setting live is a model change: it needs the approvals in
# docs/AI_ANALYSIS_MRM.md first.
#AECB_AI_BRIEF=coming_soon

# Where underwriter feedback on the AI analysis (thumbs up/down, optional
# comment) is appended, one JSON line per vote. Must be OUTSIDE the
# application directory; created 0700 with the file 0600. Leave unset to
# switch feedback off. Only used where the AI panel is live.
AECB_FEEDBACK_DIR=/var/lib/aecb-analyzer/feedback

# Developer machines only (servers run no Ollama): the local model for the
# AI Analysis. Unset means gpt-oss:120b, the target model (~65 GB; needs at
# least 96 GB of unified memory). Set gpt-oss:20b on a smaller machine. Any
# other value leaves the AI panel unavailable.
#AECB_OLLAMA_MODEL=gpt-oss:20b

# Core42 API key -- reserved. The Core42 connector is not onboarded yet and
# reads nothing; leave unset.
#AECB_CORE42_API_KEY=
